<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-22776] SQL table statistic is updated only once.</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-22776</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;To build a better plan, H2 can rely on the statistics. We can enable it with&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;
control.sh --property set --name &lt;span class=&quot;code-quote&quot;&gt;&apos;statistics. Usage. State&apos;&lt;/span&gt; --val &lt;span class=&quot;code-quote&quot;&gt;&apos;ON&apos;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;and&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-sql&quot;&gt;
&lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;ANALYZE&lt;/span&gt; MY_TABLE
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;But table statistic tends to update with CRUD only once. Despite the obsolescence threshold, by default&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;
&lt;span class=&quot;code-object&quot;&gt;int&lt;/span&gt; StatisticsObjectConfiguration#DEFAULT_OBSOLESCENCE_MAX_PERCENT = 15;
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Partition statistics obsolescence is checked every 60 seconds:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;
&lt;span class=&quot;code-object&quot;&gt;int&lt;/span&gt; IgniteStatisticsManagerImpl#OBSOLESCENCE_INTERVAL = 60;

&lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; (serverNode) {
   obsolescenceSchedule = ctx.timeout().schedule(() -&amp;gt; {
                obsolescenceBusyExecutor.execute(() -&amp;gt; processObsolescence());
   }, OBSOLESCENCE_INTERVAL * 1000, OBSOLESCENCE_INTERVAL * 1000);
}
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Regarding my research, the problem is within&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;
&lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;private&lt;/span&gt; Set&amp;lt;&lt;span class=&quot;code-object&quot;&gt;Integer&lt;/span&gt;&amp;gt; IgniteStatisticsManagerImpl#calculateObsolescencedPartitions(
        StatisticsObjectConfiguration cfg,
        IntMap&amp;lt;ObjectPartitionStatisticsObsolescence&amp;gt; parts
) {
        Set&amp;lt;&lt;span class=&quot;code-object&quot;&gt;Integer&lt;/span&gt;&amp;gt; res = &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; HashSet&amp;lt;&amp;gt;();

        parts.forEach((k, v) -&amp;gt; {
            ObjectPartitionStatisticsImpl partStat = statsRepos.getLocalPartitionStatistics(cfg.key(), k);

            &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; (partStat == &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;null&lt;/span&gt; || partStat.rowCount() == 0 ||
                (&lt;span class=&quot;code-object&quot;&gt;double&lt;/span&gt;)v.modified() * 100 / partStat.rowCount() &amp;gt; cfg.maxPartitionObsolescencePercent())
                res.add(k);
        });

        &lt;span class=&quot;code-comment&quot;&gt;// Will add even empty list of partitions to recollect just to force obsolescence info to be stored.
&lt;/span&gt;        &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; res;
}
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Where &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;
v.modified() (&lt;span class=&quot;code-object&quot;&gt;long&lt;/span&gt; ObjectPartitionStatisticsObsolescence#modified())
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;is always 0, never updates.  Probably because &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;
IgniteStatisticsManagerImpl#calculateObsolescencedPartitions#onRowUpdated(&lt;span class=&quot;code-object&quot;&gt;String&lt;/span&gt; schemaName, &lt;span class=&quot;code-object&quot;&gt;String&lt;/span&gt; objName, &lt;span class=&quot;code-object&quot;&gt;int&lt;/span&gt; partId, &lt;span class=&quot;code-object&quot;&gt;byte&lt;/span&gt;[] keyBytes) 
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;is called nowhere. But&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;
partStat.rowCount()
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;is 0 at the beginning. This is why the statistic is calculated once.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A workaroung might be setting the threshold to a negative value:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;
ANALYZE MY_TABLE WITH MAX_CHANGED_PARTITION_ROWS_PERCENT=-1
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
</description>
